UID:5726ec1ff7f83a78ad0dfe6b9c96de926e09dfc75ba72cd77c5c38278fcfa7ca@pruts-
 agenda.local
DTSTAMP:20260808T065958Z
SUMMARY:Echoes from Afar: Build your own archive
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
DTSTART:20260912T120000Z
DTEND:20260912T140000Z
DESCRIPTION:Over the past years we’ve seen an increase in censorship\, sh
 adow-banning\, and blocking of accounts across large social media platform
 s like Instagram. Many artists\, designers\, and cultural and social organ
 isations\, rely on these platforms to connect with their communities and s
 hare their stories and their work. But what if we can build our own archiv
 es and websites\, and create our own networks to share our stories\, as a 
 way to keep authorship and intention in our own hands? \n\n\nThis hybrid w
 orkshop\, led by Kexin Hong and Yiyao Wei\, begins with an introduction to
  Echoes from Afar\, an open-source\, living\, online archive that explores
  how digital infrastructures can challenge conventional forms of represent
 ation while opening up space for Asian diasporic communities to narrate th
 eir own stories. In its approach to storytelling\, the project seeks to sa
 feguard the integrity of personal narratives\, to cultivate plurality and 
 openness in how stories surface and circulate\, and to lay the groundwork 
 for a living archive that makes space for richer\, more textured forms of 
 visibility in the place of flattened or reductive images. \n\n\nIn the fir
 st part of the workshop\, participants will learn about Echoes from Afar a
 nd the basics of self-uploading and managing artworks on the platform\, so
  that participants can begin contributing their own work if they would lik
 e to. In the second part of the workshop\, we will learn about the open-so
 urce workflow behind the archive\, showing how participants can build thei
 r own websites or archives using free and accessible tools that require no
  prior coding experience. Throughout this hands-on process\, the workshop 
 will draw on AI technologies\, such as Claude\, as one of the working tool
 s that can assist website building\, while still remaining grounded in a p
 ractice of ethical care. \n\n\nNo prior coding experience is necessary and
  you do not need to be of Asian heritage to join this workshop. \n\n\nThe 
 Hmm experiments…\n\n\nThis event is part of a series of programs that we
  are developing with The Hmm\, where we give space in our studio for our c
 ommunity to explore new ideas and experiment with workshops as part of our
  public program. \n\n\nWhat you need to know\n\n📅 Date: Saturday 12 Sep
 tember 2026\n🕗 Times: 14.00 – 16.00 CEST\n📍 Location: The Hmm’s 
 studio\, NDSM-plein 125\, 1033 WC Amsterdam\, and online\n🎟 Tickets: 
 €12\,50 regular\, €9\,50 students (onsite or online)\n\nAs these works
 hops are more intimate sessions\, there is a limited supply of tickets ava
 ilable. You can find information about physical accessibility at The Hmm
 ’s studio here. \n\n💚 This programme is kindly supported by the Crea
 tive Industries Fund NL
URL:https://thehmm.nl/event/echoes-from-afar-build-your-own-archive/
CATEGORIES:The Hmm
END:VEVENT
